# Dockerfile USER directive (DS-0002): Bambuddy runs as a single-host
# Docker container where root is needed for device access and FFmpeg.
DS-0002

# util-linux hostname canonicalization (LOW, no fix available in Debian bookworm).
# Affects mount, login, libuuid1, libsmartcols1, etc. — not exploitable in container context.
CVE-2026-3184

# libtiff denial-of-service bugs (pulled in by ffmpeg, not directly used).
# No fix available in Debian bookworm.
CVE-2025-61143
CVE-2025-61144
CVE-2025-61145

# iptables --syn flag bypass (LOW, no fix available, not relevant — container doesn't use iptables).
CVE-2012-2663

# ffmpeg DVD subtitle parser heap OOB write (MEDIUM). Debian Security Tracker
# marks it "postponed" for both bookworm and trixie; no upstream fix yet.
# Not reachable in Bambuddy — ffmpeg here only ingests printer-camera RTSP
# and MJPEG/H.264/H.265 streams, never DVD/VOB files with subtitle tracks.
CVE-2026-6385

# ffmpeg AV1 decoder OOB read → DoS (MEDIUM, "minor issue" per Debian).
# Same "postponed" status in bookworm and trixie; no upstream fix yet.
# Not reachable — Bambu printer cameras emit H.264/H.265/MJPEG, not AV1.
CVE-2026-30997

# openjpeg JPEG 2000 integer overflow (LOW). No Debian fix available.
# libopenjp2-7 is pulled in transitively by ffmpeg but Bambuddy never
# decodes JPEG 2000 files (printer thumbnails are PNG, camera is MJPEG/H.264).
CVE-2026-6192

# zlib gz_write() heap overflow after a failed write() (HIGH). No fixed
# zlib1g in Debian trixie yet. Not reachable: the bug is in the gz* file API
# (gzopen/gzwrite), which nothing in the image uses for its data. Python's
# gzip and zlib modules, Pillow and ffmpeg all go through deflate/inflate.
# Remove this line once Debian ships the fix.
CVE-2026-76844

# setuptools 70.3.0 (HIGH path traversal in PackageIndex; MEDIUM sdist
# MANIFEST.in bypass). Not setuptools itself: the image has none. Trivy
# reads pip/_vendor/vendor.txt, because pip bundles setuptools'
# pkg_resources module; neither package_index nor the sdist command is
# part of what pip bundles. Remove once pip bundles setuptools >= 83.
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890

# golang.org/x/net/html in the tailscale and tailscaled binaries (HIGH DoS
# and MEDIUM XSS via crafted HTML). Tailscale 1.104.7, the newest release,
# is still built with x/net 0.60.0 (fixed in 0.62.0). Not reachable:
# Bambuddy only runs `tailscale status` / `tailscale cert` against the
# host's socket, which parses no HTML. Remove once Tailscale ships
# x/net >= 0.62.0.
CVE-2026-78661
CVE-2026-97045
